{"version":3,"kind":"Notebook","sha256":"d2e385271a404f3883db95202bfd79ab4b6953cb1770b583291889fe8a023e09","slug":"notebooks.downscaling-overview","location":"/notebooks/09_downscaling_overview.ipynb","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Temporal downscaling: 6h native steps to 1h","content_includes_title":false,"kernelspec":{"name":"e2s-gpu","display_name":"Python (e2s GPU)","language":"python"},"jupytext":{},"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"cgroll","family":"cgroll"},"name":"cgroll","id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"github":"https://github.com/cgroll/e2s-examples","copyright":"2026","numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"source_url":"https://github.com/cgroll/e2s-examples/blob/main/book/notebooks/09_downscaling_overview.ipynb","edit_url":"https://github.com/cgroll/e2s-examples/edit/main/book/notebooks/09_downscaling_overview.ipynb","thumbnail":"/e2s-examples/build/meteogram_t2m_munich-b993516a748a52db11b8424b8a40dbf2.png","exports":[{"format":"ipynb","filename":"09_downscaling_overview.ipynb","url":"/e2s-examples/build/09_downscaling_overv-86f922868a42a46ca892ab8b3a128bfd.ipynb"}]},"widgets":{},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InterpModAFNO","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"FmLygRRf5r"},{"type":"text","value":" wraps SFNO (a 6h-native prognostic model) and inserts 5\nAFNO-interpolated steps between each pair of SFNO’s own 6h outputs,\nproducing an hourly forecast. Crucially, the steps at the 6h boundaries\naren’t touched by the interpolation model - they’re SFNO’s own output,\npassed straight through. So within the single hourly zarr this experiment\nwrites, every 6th lead-time step is a genuine model prediction and\neverything in between is AFNO-synthesized.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"